# 1942 PSG filters and mix -- netlist converted from MAME
#
# Couriersud's netlist of 1942's audio mix: the two AY-3-8910s on sheet 3/8, 1PSG at A11
# and 2PSG at A10, each with three channels into the main amp sheet. MAME feeds each
# channel in through a 1K resistor from +5V that stands for the AY's own output (R_AY1_1
# ... R_AY2_3, AY 1 channel 1 being the sheet's 1PSGA); those are ports here, named as the
# sheet names the lines. Each channel has its own 10K load to ground (R11-R16), coupling
# capacitor (CC7-CC12) and 220K mixing resistor (R2-R7); the mix goes to the volume pot VR
# and through CC6 to the MB3731 bridge amplifier at A1, where MAME's netlist ends.
#
# Source: MAME mame0289 (commit f34f02505e32), src/mame/capcom/nl_1942.cpp,
# NETLIST_START(1942). Licence BSD-3-Clause by the file's own header (line 1),
# copyright-holders Couriersud (line 2).
# https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mamedev/mame/mame0289/src/mame/capcom/nl_1942.cpp
# Converted by tools/mame_netlist.py; checked by tools/build_board_nets.py.
#
# What the conversion means. MAME's netlists are written to be simulated, so this is a
# second reading of the sheet by someone else, not a read of it: designators and pin
# numbers are MAME's unless the notes say the sheet was read to correct them. Names on
# `label` lines are MAME's, which mostly follow the sheet's with Q for an overbar; `net`
# is used only for the supply rails. A `port` is a net that leaves what this file
# describes -- a signal from the CPU or the other board, a cabinet control, or a source
# MAME simulates with a stand-in rather than the circuit.
#
#   net NAME: PIN ...     a supply rail
#   label NAME: PIN ...   a net MAME names
#   wire PIN PIN ...      an unnamed connection
#   port NAME: PIN ...    a net that leaves this file (see above)
#   nc PIN ...            a pin with nothing attached
#   parallel PIN ...      outputs the board sums on one node by design
#   value REF VALUE       a passive's value, in the unit MAME's own macro uses
#
# PIN is DESIGNATOR.NUMBER. Diode pin 1 is the cathode; transistors keep B, C and E;
# MAME does not record which way round an electrolytic goes, so C pins are MAME's 1/2.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Undone: what MAME does to simulate the board that the board does not do
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Port names from the main amp sheet (84100-01A-2 4/8), for the amplifier pins MAME's netlist ends on:
#   CC6 and R1 meet at the MB3731's input, A1 pin 1: CC6.2 (A1_1)
#   R1's other end and CC3 (220uF) are on A1 pin 5: CC3.1 (A1_5)
# line 19: 1PSGA is not a part -- the AY-3-8910's own output resistance on 1PSGA, which MAME draws as a 1K resistor from +5V (R_AY1_1)
# line 20: 1PSGB is not a part -- the AY-3-8910's own output resistance on 1PSGB, which MAME draws as a 1K resistor from +5V (R_AY1_2)
# line 21: 1PSGC is not a part -- the AY-3-8910's own output resistance on 1PSGC, which MAME draws as a 1K resistor from +5V (R_AY1_3)
# line 22: 2PSGA is not a part -- the AY-3-8910's own output resistance on 2PSGA, which MAME draws as a 1K resistor from +5V (R_AY2_1)
# line 23: 2PSGB is not a part -- the AY-3-8910's own output resistance on 2PSGB, which MAME draws as a 1K resistor from +5V (R_AY2_2)
# line 24: 2PSGC is not a part -- the AY-3-8910's own output resistance on 2PSGC, which MAME draws as a 1K resistor from +5V (R_AY2_3)
#
# Compared with the MAIN AMP. sheet, 84100-01A-2 4/8 (doc 27d4fd762a04, PDF p. 4; the scan
# is legible throughout), and sheet 3/8 for where the PSG lines come from, on 2026-10-20:
# every net and value in this file agrees. The channels are 2PSGC through R13, CC7 and R2;
# 2PSGB R15, CC8, R3; 2PSGA R11, CC9, R4; 1PSGC R12, CC10, R5; 1PSGB R14, CC11, R6; 1PSGA
# R16, CC12, R7 -- '10K x 6', '10uF/16V x 6', '220K x 6' -- into VR (2K, pin 1 the mix, 2
# the wiper, 3 ground), CC6 10uF to A1 pin 1, R1 100K from there to pin 5, and CC3 220uF
# from pin 5 to ground. On sheet 3/8 the PSG lines leave the AY-3-8910s' analogue outputs
# (C on pin 38, B on 3, A on 4) with nothing between them and this sheet. On every
# electrolytic here the + end is MAME's pin 1 except CC6, whose + end faces the amplifier
# (pin 2).
#
# On the sheet and not in MAME: the MB3731 at A1 -- CC5 10uF on pin 4, pins 3, 7 and the
# tab to ground, CC1 and CC2 (100uF) bootstrapping pins 12-10 and 9-8, the bridged outputs
# 10 and 8 to edge pins 6/F and 5/E with C1-C3 (0.15uF Mylar, '154 x 3') -- and its +12V on
# pin 11, with C4 0.1uF and CC4 470uF, from edge pins 3/C and 4/D.


value R1 100000
value R2 220000
value R3 220000
value R4 220000
value R5 220000
value R6 220000
value R7 220000
value R11 10000
value R12 10000
value R13 10000
value R14 10000
value R15 10000
value R16 10000
value VR 2000
value CC3 220e-6
value CC6 10e-6
value CC7 10e-6
value CC8 10e-6
value CC9 10e-6
value CC10 10e-6
value CC11 10e-6
value CC12 10e-6

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supplies
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
net GND: CC3.2 R11.2 R12.2 R13.2 R14.2 R15.2 R16.2 VR.3

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AY 8910 internal resistors
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
port 2PSGC: CC7.1 R13.1  # in MAME: 2PSGC, not part: the AY-3-8910's own output resistance on 2PSGC, which MAME draws as a 1K resistor from +5V (R_AY2_3)
wire CC7.2 R2.1
port 2PSGB: CC8.1 R15.1  # in MAME: 2PSGB, not part: the AY-3-8910's own output resistance on 2PSGB, which MAME draws as a 1K resistor from +5V (R_AY2_2)
wire CC8.2 R3.1
port 2PSGA: CC9.1 R11.1  # in MAME: 2PSGA, not part: the AY-3-8910's own output resistance on 2PSGA, which MAME draws as a 1K resistor from +5V (R_AY2_1)
wire CC9.2 R4.1
port 1PSGC: CC10.1 R12.1  # in MAME: 1PSGC, not part: the AY-3-8910's own output resistance on 1PSGC, which MAME draws as a 1K resistor from +5V (R_AY1_3)
wire CC10.2 R5.1
port 1PSGB: CC11.1 R14.1  # in MAME: 1PSGB, not part: the AY-3-8910's own output resistance on 1PSGB, which MAME draws as a 1K resistor from +5V (R_AY1_2)
wire CC11.2 R6.1
port 1PSGA: CC12.1 R16.1  # in MAME: 1PSGA, not part: the AY-3-8910's own output resistance on 1PSGA, which MAME draws as a 1K resistor from +5V (R_AY1_1)
wire CC12.2 R7.1
wire R2.2 R3.2 R4.2 R5.2 R6.2 R7.2 VR.1
wire CC6.1 VR.2
port A1_1: CC6.2 R1.1  # the MB3731 power amplifier's input (A1 pin 1), which MAME does not simulate
port A1_5: CC3.1 R1.2  # MB3731 pin 5, held by R1 and CC3; the amplifier is not in MAME

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pins with nothing attached
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
